  "headline": "The Blue City",
  "short_description": "Jodhpur's indigo-washed old town sits beneath the imposing Mehrangarh Fort on the edge of the Thar Desert.",
  "about": "Founded in 1459 by Rao Jodha, Jodhpur is dominated by the massive Mehrangarh Fort and known for its blue-painted Brahmin quarter.\n\nLocated on the edge of the Thar Desert in western Rajasthan.\n\nKnown for Marwari folk music, leatherwork and the distinctive blue-washed old city houses.\n\nPredominantly Hindu with significant Jain merchant heritage.",
  "history": "Capital of the former Marwar kingdom, a key stop on historic trade routes between Delhi and Gujarat.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Jodhpur Airport (airport)\n- Jodhpur Junction (railway)\n- Jodhpur Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Marwari, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2 days",
